---
const deliverables = [
  {
    lead: 'A current-state architecture assessment.',
    body: 'What the system actually is, as opposed to what the documentation and the org chart say it is.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'A ranked risk register.',
    body: 'Every material risk, ordered by expected cost, with the evidence behind each ranking.',
  },
  {
    lead: 'A sequenced modernization roadmap.',
    body: 'What to do first, what it unblocks, and what can safely wait.',
  },
];
---

<section class="mb-16 max-w-2xl">
  <h2 class="font-mono text-lg mb-6 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2 text-white">A fixed-fee technical assessment</h2>

  <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
    Most teams already know their system is slow and risky to change. What's missing is a defensible account of why, what it will cost, and what to do first.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-4 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
    Three to four weeks of engaged work, fixed fee. You get:
  </p>

  <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4">
    {deliverables.map((item) => (
      <li class="border border-brand-slate p-6">
        <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
          <span class="text-white">{item.lead}</span> {item.body}
        </p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <p class="mt-6 text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">
    Implementation is a separate conversation. The assessment stands on its own and is useful whether or not I do the work that follows.
  </p>
</section>
